3. Removed the `as any` from the SessionProvider since our mock data now matches the expected structure
4. Kept the role assignment using UserPermissionRole enum

The main issue was that the session structure wasn't matching what next-auth expects. The `useSession` hook in the WebhooksView component expects to find the user data directly on the session object, not nested under a `data` property.

This should resolve the "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'role')" error because the user object with its role will now be available in the correct location within the session structure.

